I've just started running a small(ish) NetHack server for readers of
the online comic strip User Friendly. However, I've straight away
noticed a couple of problems.
First, occasionally a nethack process will become detached from its
terminal, and start consuming vast amounts of CPU time - as much as it
can get its hands on, in fact. I'm sure I've heard about this before,
but I'm not sure how to prevent it.
Second, when I terminate one of these processes, it leaves behind its
lockfiles, and after a while NetHack complains there are too many
NetHack processes running, and refuses to allow new people in (Is
there a way to extend this limit, by the way?)
Is anyone aware of solutions or workarounds for these issues?

